<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0732">Remark <span data-tag="0732">9.7.8.25</span> <span class="named">(Tensor Products of Idempotents)</span>.</a> Let $\mathbb {K}$ be a collection of simplicial sets and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}'$ be $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete idempotents. Then the $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete tensor product $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\otimes _{ \mathbb {K} } \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}'$ is also a $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete idempotent. Moreover a $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is a $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete $(\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\otimes _{ \mathbb {K} } \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}')$-module if and only if it is both a $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$-module and a $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}'$-module. It follows that the equivalence class $[\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\otimes _{ \mathbb {K} } \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}']$ is a greatest lower bound for $[ \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}]$ and $[ \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}' ]$, with respect to the partial ordering of Remark <a data-tag="072Z" href="/tag/072Z">9.7.8.22</a>. </p>
